cs5,0$

1,cs11$ Basidiocarp sessile or with a lateral stem $ Group A
1,2 $ Basidiocarp with a central to eccentric stem
2,0 $ Volva present, annulus absent $ Volvariella bombycina
2,3 $ Volva absent, annulus present or not
3,cs15 $ Annulus present on upper portion of stipe $ Group E
3,4 $ Annulus absent on upper portion of stipe
4,5 $ Edge of gills even
4,7 $ Edge of gills notched or toothed like a saw or appearing eroded or torn
5,cs12 $ Gills conspicuously decurrent to subdecurrent $ Group B
5,6 $ Gills free or if attached, not decurrent
6,cs14 $ Spore print purple-brown to black $ Group D
6,cs13 $ Spore print white to buff or pinkish-salmon $ Group C
7,0 $ Spore print buff, cap pinkish-brown to brown, smooth; gills pinkish brown $ Lentinellus omphalodes
7,8 $ Spore print pinkish or white
8,0 $ Spore print pinkish, cap bluish to violet, gill edges dark blue-black $ Leptonia serrulata
8,0 $ Spore print white, cap brownish-grey, streaked with dark, radial fibers; gills white,may appear torn or eroded; white rhizomorphs at base of stalk $ Megacollybia platyphylla

